    {
      "id": "d5c440e1-f262-4fa0-88a1-05c7d6ca0616",
      "name": "What is MCP and Why Should You Care",
      "path": "WWW / Blog / What is MCP and Why Should You Care",
      "docTypeId": "0ab70f91-ccfb-4d5f-a5e3-b69dacb484bb",
      "templateId": "56b2436f-b412-465c-8549-e76e1cd3d0bb",
      "state": "Published",
      "domains": [],
      "values": [
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "pageTitle",
          "value": "What is MCP and Why Should You Care?"
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.BlockGrid",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "blocks",
          "value": {
            "layout": {
              "Umbraco.BlockGrid": [
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "fb6431aa-6d53-4fb8-8a4b-b0d0510b75d9",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "4e4d57d2-4b4d-4f59-a4b1-42ab35e127ca",
                  "settingsKey": null
                }
              ]
            },
            "contentData": [
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "c9ed7cd9-779e-4c46-bf22-ef7c930831d1",
                "key": "fb6431aa-6d53-4fb8-8a4b-b0d0510b75d9",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "heading",
                    "value": "What is MCP and Why Should You Care?"
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextArea",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "text",
                    "value": "The Model Context Protocol is changing how AI systems interact with tools and data. Here is everything you need to know."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "9a051694-c6f1-4e3e-8a56-e048de081767",
                "key": "4e4d57d2-4b4d-4f59-a4b1-42ab35e127ca",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "content",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<h2>What is MCP?</h2><p>The Model Context Protocol (MCP) is an open standard that lets AI models connect securely to the tools, data, and workflows they need — without custom integrations or fragile plumbing.</p><p>Think of it as a USB-C port for AI: one protocol, any tool, any provider. Instead of wiring each LLM to each tool individually, MCP gives both sides a common language to negotiate capabilities, exchange context, and execute actions.</p><h2>Why does it matter?</h2><p>Before MCP, every AI-tool integration was bespoke. You wrote a custom plugin for OpenAI, another for Anthropic, another for your internal API. Each broke when either side updated. Developers spent more time maintaining connectors than building features.</p><p>MCP changes that. It standardises:</p><ul><li><strong>Resource access</strong> — fetching files, database rows, or API responses</li><li><strong>Tool execution</strong> — safely running actions with human oversight</li><li><strong>Context windows</strong> — streaming results back so the model stays grounded</li></ul><p>The result? Faster development, fewer bugs, and integrations that work across every major LLM provider.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "settingsData": [],
            "expose": [
