    {
      "id": "f7e2a2d3-2d51-4f95-ac80-c2ebe698a6ce",
      "name": "Building with MCP A Practical Guide",
      "path": "WWW / Blog / Building with MCP A Practical Guide",
      "docTypeId": "0ab70f91-ccfb-4d5f-a5e3-b69dacb484bb",
      "templateId": "56b2436f-b412-465c-8549-e76e1cd3d0bb",
      "state": "Published",
      "domains": [],
      "values": [
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "pageTitle",
          "value": "Building with MCP: A Practical Guide"
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.BlockGrid",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "blocks",
          "value": {
            "layout": {
              "Umbraco.BlockGrid": [
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "8bab2431-c75d-4d9f-a176-6c40634b11cc",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "93c6064c-9bf1-473e-9d73-8e3ff8d97357",
                  "settingsKey": null
                }
              ]
            },
            "contentData": [
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "c9ed7cd9-779e-4c46-bf22-ef7c930831d1",
                "key": "8bab2431-c75d-4d9f-a176-6c40634b11cc",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "heading",
                    "value": "Building with MCP: A Practical Guide"
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextArea",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "text",
                    "value": "Learn how to build MCP servers from scratch and connect them to any LLM in minutes."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "9a051694-c6f1-4e3e-8a56-e048de081767",
                "key": "93c6064c-9bf1-473e-9d73-8e3ff8d97357",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "content",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<h2>Getting Started</h2><p>Building an MCP server is surprisingly straightforward. The protocol is transport-agnostic — you can serve it over stdio (for local tools) or HTTP+SSE (for remote services). The official SDKs for TypeScript, Python, Java, and Kotlin handle the protocol mechanics so you focus on your actual tools.</p><h2>Your First Tool</h2><p>An MCP server exposes <strong>tools</strong> — functions the AI can call with your approval. Each tool has a name, description, and typed parameters. The LLM decides which tool to invoke based on the description, so clear naming is essential.</p><p>Here is what a simple weather tool looks like:</p><pre><code>@Tool(description: \"Get current weather\")\nfun getWeather(\n    @ToolParam(description: \"City name\") city: String\n): String { ... }</code></pre><h2>Resources and Context</h2><p>MCP also provides <strong>resources</strong> — read-only data the AI can pull in. Files, database queries, API responses — anything that helps the model stay accurate. Resources update in real-time, so the AI always works with fresh data.</p><p>Together, tools and resources mean the AI can read your database schema, then write a query — all through one protocol. That is the power of MCP.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "settingsData": [],
            "expose": [
